# What the Vercel CLI may upload from this working directory.
#
# `vercel --prod` uploads the LOCAL FOLDER, not the git repository, and it does
# not read .gitignore. Without this file it tried to send:
#
#   For website.pptx                   425 MB
#   _source-assets/For website.pptx    425 MB
#   _source-assets/AIS Intro.pptx       10 MB
#   output/pdf/*.pdf                    29 MB
#
# The first of those is the source deck, which carries patient identifiers
# burned into images on several slides; the third is the corporate deck, marked
# "Confidential information — not for public distribution". The 100 MB per-file
# limit aborted the upload before either deck landed, but that was luck, not
# design: AIS Intro.pptx is well under the limit and would have gone up.
#
# Nothing here is needed to build the site. Deploying from the Git integration
# instead of the CLI avoids the problem entirely, since Vercel then builds from
# the repository, where .gitignore already excludes all of it.

# Build and dependency output — Vercel installs and builds its own.
node_modules
.next
.git

# Source decks and unreviewed originals. Never deployed, never needed at build.
_source-assets
*.pptx
*.ppt

# Review artifacts from working sessions.
output
tmp
.claude

# Raw clinical exports with burned-in identifiers, and full-resolution capture
# originals. Both are already gitignored; named again here because this file is
# read independently of .gitignore.
public/case-library
public/fundus/OD/aligned

# Local env pulled by `vercel env pull`. Production values come from the
# project's own environment settings, never from an uploaded file.
.env*

*.tsbuildinfo
